HL_data/

# Generated parameter/output JSON files. Tracking them turned every commit
# into calibration churn and made real changes hard to see in a diff.
scripts/*.json

# The user_data/ rules that used to live here went with the freqtrade trader
# (retired 2026-08-25, tag freqtrade-trader-final): the estimator's parameter
# snapshots, mm_debug.jsonl, param_update.lock, the tradesv3 databases and the
# compose override. Nothing writes any of those now.

# Local secrets. The freqtrade API-server credentials this held are dead, but
# the rule stays: a .env must never be committable regardless of what writes it.
.env

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# AI review bundles generated by scripts/bundle_project.py
project_bundle*.md

# Reference books and other large binaries stay local. The Cartea-Jaimungal
# textbook was committed once by accident (32 MB, and not ours to
# redistribute) and had to be stripped from history with git-filter-repo.
docs/*.pdf
# ...except our own writing. This one is ~0.7 MB, is generated from
# docs/spread_calculation.tex in this repo, and the README links to it, so it
# has to be committed or the link is dead for everyone but us.
!docs/spread_calculation.pdf

# LaTeX build artefacts
docs/*.aux
docs/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/*.fls
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.synctex.gz

# Rust engine build/runtime artifacts. Source, Cargo.lock and example profiles
# remain tracked; account state and live calibration output are local evidence.
rust_live/target/
rust_live/fuzz/target/
rust_live/run/
rust_live/config/local.toml
rust_live/config/*.acceptance.local.toml
rust_live/config/*.state.json
rust_live/config/*.snapshot.json
rust_live/reports/

# Real Hyperliquid credentials are local-only. The dummy template remains
# tracked and is safe to copy before replacing its values locally.
hyperliquid.env
!hyperliquid.env.example
scripts/guard_study_tapes/
scripts/guard_study/run/

# The lockfree ring-buffer export and its patch. Untracked in a583d55 because a
# 19 MB zip does not belong in history, but never ignored -- so they sat in
# every `git status` as untracked, one careless `git add -A` away from going
# back in. The source they hold is in the tree; these are the export artefacts.
Cartea-Jaimungal_MARKET_MAKING_RUST_HYPERLIQUID_LOCKFREE.zip
Cartea-Jaimungal_lockfree_ring_buffers.patch
